1
00:00:05,200 --> 00:00:10,000
This is a 2009 Asus K50IJ. Its disk controller makes every Linux hang at boot.

2
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:15,000
Now it has no OS: it pulls a 41 KB bare-metal kernel over the network at boot, then the cable can be unplugged. It keeps living.

3
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:20,500
Left: a worm in a petri dish. Right: its brain - 302 neurons, 10,193 synapses, all from the public OpenWorm connectome.

4
00:00:20,500 --> 00:00:26,000
Press H to poke its head: touch neurons ALM/AVM fire, activity travels along the wires to the command neurons, the motor area turns magenta - it reverses.

5
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:31,500
Every line that lights up is a real synapse used in that step. Not an animation: a state the CPU computes 120 times a second.

6
00:00:31,500 --> 00:00:37,500
Each body segment bends by the activation of its own dorsal and ventral muscles; the orange glow is food, and it crawls up the gradient.

7
00:00:37,500 --> 00:00:46,000
All of it runs on this 2009 dual-core CPU: int16 fixed point, SSE2 multiply-add, two brain steps per frame, not one line of OS code.

8
00:00:46,200 --> 00:00:50,000
What follows is the same kernel in an unattended QEMU run - the picture is identical to the real machine.

9
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:54,500
Free crawling: the forward command neurons AVB stay active, B-class motor neurons drive the muscles, the body makes a travelling wave.

10
00:00:54,800 --> 00:01:00,000
Poke the head: the ALM/AVM to AVD/AVA escape circuit takes over, A-class motor neurons fire, the worm backs up and turns.

11
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:04,000
FWD / BWD in the status line are the live spike counts of the forward and backward motor neurons.

12
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:09,000
Poke the tail: PLM to PVC to AVB - it surges forward and does not reverse.

13
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:14,000
Drop food: ASEL / ASER sense the concentration rising and falling, and it follows the gradient into the glow.

14
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:20,500
On the food: the pharyngeal neurons NSM / MC are driven, it slows down; the blue dot in the head is the pharynx pumping - 150 pumps and the food is gone.

15
00:01:20,500 --> 00:01:25,500
Poke the head again and it reverses again - every response comes from the same connectome.

16
00:01:25,500 --> 00:01:29,500
This is a qualitative cartoon: the wiring is real, the neuron dynamics are a simplified integrate-and-fire model.
